 /* scratch: a FIXED DECIMAL subscript — is the value unscaled before it
    addresses the array? (found while measuring WS-S1)

    The scaled form is now rejected (ADR-277): a subscript must be of an
    integer type, so `fixed dec(5,2)` is diagnosed with

        error: a subscript must be of an integer type, not FIXED DECIMAL(5,2)

    The compiler used to take the stored (scaled) value as the index, so
    `i = 2.00` addressed element 200 of a three-element array: a false
    SUBSCRIPTRANGE trap with the checks on, and an out-of-bounds access
    through an `inbounds` GEP without them. The scale-0 form below is the
    one that carries an integer, and it selects the right element. */
 probe: procedure options(main);
   declare a(1:3) fixed dec(5,0);
   declare i fixed dec(5,0);
   declare x fixed dec(9,0);
   declare fails fixed bin(31);
   fails = 0;
   a(1) = 10;
   a(2) = 20;
   a(3) = 30;
   i = 2;
   x = a(i);
   put skip list(x);
   if x ^= 20 then fails = fails + 1;
   put skip list(fails);
 end;
